@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`createTaskList` keeps tasks in a `Map` keyed by title. Domain code may not read the clock, use randomness or throw.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Unique, stable ids; id-or-title lookup through one shared path.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Persistence across lists, or ids unique across different lists.
+- Changing `list` ordering or `summarize`.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- **Ids from a per-list counter** (`"t1"`, `"t2"`, …), never decremented, so removed ids are not reused. Alternatives (UUID, timestamps) break the no-randomness/no-clock rule.
+- **Id wins over title** when a string is both the id of one task and the title of another; ids are checked first, then titles. A lookup helper `resolve(ref)` is used by `find`, `get` (id only) and all mutators.
+- **Keep the title-keyed map** for duplicate-title detection, and add an id-keyed `Map<string, Task>` index maintained in `store`, `add` and `remove`.
+- `Task` gains a readonly `id`; `createTask` takes the id as a parameter, since it must not generate it.
+
+## Risks / Trade-offs
+
+- A task titled like another task's id (e.g. "t2") is reachable by title only if no task has that id → acceptable; the id is the stable reference.
