+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Tasks are only referred to by title, and a title changes when the task is renamed. The app needs a stable
+reference that survives renaming.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Every task gets a unique string `id`, assigned by `add` and never changed afterwards (rename, tag, complete, reopen keep it).
+- The task list gets `get(id)`, returning a `Result<Task>` (`not-found` when no task has that id).
+- `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept a task's id as well as its title.
+- Ids are generated without clock or randomness (domain rule): a per-list counter.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `task-identity`: unique, stable task ids and lookup of a task by id or title.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/domain/task.ts` (`Task` gains `id`), `src/domain/list.ts` (id assignment, `get`, id-or-title lookup).
+- Public `Task` type exported from `src/index.ts` gains a field; existing tests that deep-compare a task need the `id`.
+- No new dependency.
